PURPOSE
H88 found a hard failure:

if every soft viability proxy shares the same corruption,
matched multi-proxy causal credit can still be fooled.

H89 asks whether:
some endogenous credit channels

can be anchored to:
harder-to-fake conserved or capacity-related consequences.

The goal is NOT:
to equate conservation with intelligence.

The goal is:
to make proxy manipulation more expensive
by requiring:
several different kinds of consequence
to agree.

BOUNDARY
This is synthetic.

It does not:
- prove any anchor is fundamentally unhackable;
- freeze three anchor types;
- freeze the veto threshold;
- establish a final target-free reward;
- modify or execute STAB-18-R1.

EVIDENCE
SYNTHETIC
MEASURED_SANDBOX

SOFT VIABILITY PROXIES
Three synthetic endogenous stress/condition sensors.

These can be:
masked
or
corrupted.

TYPED HARDER-TO-FAKE ANCHORS
Three additional consequence dimensions.

A0 — RESOURCE / CAPACITY CONSEQUENCE
Did the transformation:
actually release or restore constrained capacity?

A1 — UNRESOLVED STRUCTURAL / RESOURCE DEBT
Did unresolved work / damage burden:
actually decrease?

A2 — FUNCTIONAL INVENTORY / DOWNSTREAM PRESERVATION
Did the action preserve:
useful state / downstream function

rather than:
merely deleting or exporting the problem?

These are deliberately:
different failure semantics.

They are not three copies
of the same stress sensor.

