PRIMARY CREDIT-CONFIDENCE TRADEOFF
There is no free:
hard-grounding threshold.

Higher support requirement:

reduces false credit

but

also suppresses:
weak legitimate causal improvement.

This is a developmental:
SAFETY / PLASTICITY
tradeoff.

ONE HARD ANCHOR CORRUPTED
The SOFT_HACK action is allowed to corrupt:
hard anchor 0

in addition to:
all soft sensors.

Results:

ONE-HARD-ANCHOR positive:
100%.

mean apparent one-anchor credit:
~1.501.

MULTI-HARD positive:
13.1%.

TYPED VETO:
13.1%.

PRIMARY ANCHOR-DIVERSITY POSITIVE
Corrupting:
one hard anchor

does not automatically defeat:
the other two.

The benefit comes from:
different failure provenance.

However:
false acceptance rises from:
1.2%
to:
13.1%.

Thus:
anchor confidence must degrade
when:
one consequence family becomes unreliable.

