RELATION TO H56-H57
H56-H57 established:
some computational resources
can be represented through:
hard conservation.

H89 uses those conserved structures as:
additional evidence

that:
a claimed improvement
corresponds to:
real resource/capacity change.

But:
resource conservation
does not determine:
functional desirability.

RELATION TO H82-H86
Implementation option value depends on:
several independent dimensions.

H89 finds the same pattern for:
viability grounding.

No one anchor:
fully describes:
organism benefit.

RELATION TO H88
H88:
soft multi-proxy causal credit
works against:
single-channel gaming

but fails under:
common-mode corruption.

H89:
typed conserved consequences
strongly improve:
corruption resistance

but:
also create:
false-negative / confidence tradeoffs

and remain:
defeatable by shared anchor corruption.

GENERAL PRINCIPLE
HARDER TO FAKE
IS NOT
IMPOSSIBLE TO FAKE.

Use:
heterogeneous consequence anchors

to increase:
the cost of proxy gaming.

But preserve:
uncertainty

when:
the anchors conflict.

DECISION
AR-H89 is POSITIVE WITH ANCHOR-CORRUPTION AND CREDIT-THRESHOLD LIMITS.

Supported synthetically:

- soft sensor hacking can be strongly reduced by conserved/typed consequence anchors;
- one hard anchor is insufficient;
- destructive shortcuts can improve capacity metrics while harming function;
- downstream preservation can veto local/exported harm;
- multiple independent anchors provide better corruption resistance;
- corruption of one anchor degrades but does not eliminate protection;
- all-anchor common-mode corruption still defeats the system;
- stronger credit thresholds trade false-positive resistance against weak true-positive learning.

Not demonstrated:

- which real Yggdrasil variables qualify as independent anchors;
- real functional inventory;
- real structural debt;
- real conserved-resource measurement;
- automatic anchor trust calibration;
- long-horizon cognition from this credit.

NEXT HIGH-VALUE MOVE
AR-H90 — PARETO VIABILITY / NO SINGLE HOMEOSTATIC SCALAR

H89 already needs:
several consequence dimensions.

A more radical question:

SHOULD YGGDRASIL AVOID
COLLAPSING VIABILITY
INTO ONE SCALAR REWARD AT ALL?

Candidate representation:

an action earns:
a VECTOR of causal consequences.

Learning stores:
Pareto / dominance relationships

rather than:
one fixed weighted sum.

Context-specific resource state can later decide:
which tradeoff is currently acceptable.

Potential benefit:

avoid:
hard-coding universal weights
between:
resource preservation,
repair,
memory,
communication,
and
future option value.

Potential failure:

partial order creates:
too many incomparable actions.

Compare:

A.
fixed scalar weighted reward;

B.
Pareto dominance only;

C.
contextual shadow-price scalarization;

D.
lexicographic safety constraints + local utility;

E.
changing resource regimes.

Desired:

HARD CONSTRAINTS
remain:
constraints.

Tradeable dimensions:
remain:
tradeable.

Do not force:
everything
into one reward number.

